name: sim.rmlStep
description:
luaSynopsis: If you wish to use this function in a blocking mode, consider using sim.moveToPose and sim.moveToConfig instead.
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. handle: the handle of the object created via simRMLPos or simRMLVel.
2. timeStep: the cycle time
3. newPosVelAccl: the new position, velocity and acceleration (output values). Values are arranged as {pos1,pos2,..,posN,vel1,vel2,..,velN,accel1,accel2,..,accelN}
4. auxData: can be nullptr. Otherwise in/out extension data. The first byte indicates how many additional in/out values we wish to set/get. Following auxiliary values can be set/get:
5. reserved: reserved for future extensions. Set to nullptr.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. -1 in case of an error, otherwise the return value of function RMLPosition or RMLVelocity in the Reflexxes Motion Library:
2. 1: final state reached
3. 0: final state not yet reached
4. -100: RML_ERROR_INVALID_INPUT_VALUES
5. -101: RML_ERROR_EXECUTION_TIME_CALCULATION
6. -102: RML_ERROR_SYNCHRONIZATION
7. -103: RML_ERROR_NUMBER_OF_DOFS
8. -104: RML_ERROR_NO_PHASE_SYNCHRONIZATION
9. -105: RML_ERROR_NULL_POINTER
10. -106: RML_ERROR_EXECUTION_TIME_TOO_BIG
11. value 1 : Bytes 2-9 (double): returns the synchronization time (the time needed to reach the desired state. This time does not include the cycle time of the current call to simRMLStep)
replacedBy:
- name: step, class: RuckigPosition, file: RuckigPosition_step.method
- name: data, class: RuckigPosition, file: RuckigPosition_data.method
- name: step, class: RuckigVelocity, file: RuckigVelocity_step.method
- name: data, class: RuckigVelocity, file: RuckigVelocity_data.method
